    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #289\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-262-mailbox-heartbeat-fix-01-01-guard-soft-thr_jugfimq72c`.\n\n## Summary\n\n`passesItemRelationFilter` (in `backend/packages/data/src/scheduler/itemRelationFilter.ts`), which gates the `newEmail` heartbeat's `core.agentRun` action on a fired item's related-folder properties, had two bugs:\n\n1. **No partition pruning**: `items` is `PARTITION BY LIST (database_id)`, but the query joined `items related` purely on `id`, forcing Postgres to scan every database's partition instead of pruning to the one the related item actually lives in.\n2. **No soft-delete guard**: the query didn't check `deleted_at`, so a soft-deleted folder (e.g. a removed Junk folder) could still count toward the `include`/`exclude` sets.\n\n**Fix**: resolve the related item's `database_id` via the relation definition's other-side property (joining the small unpartitioned `properties` table) and pin it in the `items` join condition — mirroring the pattern already used in `rollup/recompute.ts` — plus add `related.deleted_at IS NULL`.\n\n**Test coverage**:\n- `newEmailHeartbeat.test.ts` — soft-deletes a Junk folder mid-flight and verifies the `newEmail` action still fires once the deleted folder no longer blocks it.\n- `itemRelationFilter.test.ts` (new) — runs `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, FORMAT JSON)` against a database seeded with ~19 `items_p_*` partitions and asserts only the related item's own partition is actually executed at runtime, verifying the partition-pruning fix.\n\nBoth review findings from the earlier CI pass (missing join predicate risking a cross-item match, unguarded non-null assertion) were fixed in the test file.\n\nThe branch was rebased onto the latest `develop` (which added `6e12a2f`, a CI check for colliding migration ordinals) to resolve a divergence before pushing.\n\nFull test suite (25 files, 315 tests) and workspace-wide `tsc --noEmit` pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
